### MEDUSA API — Persistent Audit Events
### VS Code REST Client (.http)
### Prerequisites:
### - API running locally and Alembic migrations applied (alembic upgrade head).
### - @adminEmail must belong to an existing account whose database role is "admin".
### - @participantEmail must belong to an existing participant account.
### - Run requests in order. Run the submission/challenge .http workflow first to generate events.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@participantEmail = user2@example.com
@password = stringstring
@actorUserId = 1

### 1. Login as platform admin
# @name auditAdminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{adminEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 2. List the latest audit events (expected 200)
# @name listAuditEvents
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 3. Filter challenge submission outcomes (expected 200)
# Includes incorrect/correct submission events, if those actions have been performed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?action=challenge.submission&limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 4. Filter challenge metadata updates (expected 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?action=challenge.updated&resource_type=challenge&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 5. Filter competition status changes (expected 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?action=competition.status_changed&resource_type=competition
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 6. Filter by actor user ID (replace @actorUserId with a real users.id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?actor_user_id={{actorUserId}}&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 7. Test pagination (expected 200; maximum limit is 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{auditAdminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 8. Test unauthenticated access (expected 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events

### 9. Login as a participant
# @name auditParticipantLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{participantEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 10. Test participant cannot read audit events (expected 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{auditParticipantLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Expected results / security checks
# - Requests 2–7: HTTP 200 and a JSON array (possibly empty if no matching events exist).
# - Request 8: HTTP 401.
# - Request 10: HTTP 403.
# - Submission events should contain action/outcome/resource metadata, not submitted flag values,
#   passwords, bearer tokens, or flag hashes.
# - To test event generation, run requests/medusa-submissions.http and then rerun requests 2–5.
